==Battleground==
*2 [[St. Pigge the 2nd]]s spawn, delay 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Duche]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Squire Rel]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[St. Pigge the 2nd]] spawns.
**1 [[Elizabeth the LVIth]] spawns.
**1 [[Winged Pigge]] spawns.

==Strategy==
The plan for this stage is simple: hold off the Pigges while chipping them with backliners, watching to make sure the Duches don't get in the way and halt your crowd-controlling effects. Though it's possible to cheese the stage, though it is a very slow process. You can use [[Cat God the Great (Special Cat)|Cat God the Awesome]] here, or use [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]] as a faster alternative, and use cheap, but durable meatshields like [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]], or [[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]]. Then wait for the Duches to clog-up the enemy limit of 4, and kill the base without killing any of the Duches, which will allow you to beat the stage without dealing with the deadly combo of Pigge variants.

==='''Recommended Units'''===

Any unit that targets one (or, even better, more) of the traits presented can be effective, especially crowd-controllers.
*[[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] - Almost a given here, the main goal through the battle is making sure this unit can survive for as long as possible.
*[[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]]/[[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer Cat]] - Both units have [[Immune to Weaken|Weaken Immunity]], and they work well as ranged attackers in this stage. Use Cyborg Cat if you dont have talents on Dancer. Dancer Cat is safer here if you have his [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immune]] Talent and decent levels though.
*[[Bakery Cat (Rare Cat)|Fried Chicken Cat]] - Works as one of the few units that can curse Winged Pigge, so long as you protect him. Worthwhile if you are really struggling in the higher 3 and 4 crown versions of this stage.
*[[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]] - One of the only meat shields here that work effectively. As with Talents, it can tank quite a few hits from both Pigges due to its Weaken Immunity and  [[Strong Against|Strong VS]] alien.
*[[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]] - They can demolish the Winged Pigge and their Curse helps a ton as well. However, use them carefully as Winged Pigge's higher standing distance than St. Pigge and Omni-Strike means you have to time Cafeteria well in order to hit her, likely requiring Freeze from something like the Thunderbolt Cannon.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] - With his [[Explosion]] talent unlocked, his damage per hit becomes high enough to force a knockback from Winged Pigge. This makes it possible to kill Winged Pigge with just Bahamut. Even if Bahamut doesn't kill her outright, her health should be low enough to finish her off without much trouble. Note that this only applies to {{1c}} and {{4c}}.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[:Category:Cats with Weaken Immunity|Weaken Immune Ubers]] - Any Uber that has decent range and Weaken Immune is good here as they can sit comfortably behind a Wave Shield and deal damage to the Winged Pigge and Elizabeth.
*[[Yamii (Uber Rare Cat)|Yaminora]] - Yammi's range on top of [[Wave Shield]] and Weaken make a very safe way to deal with this stage, He completely disables Elizabeth and make the stage a question of how to deal with Winged Pigge.
*[[Shitakiri Sparrow (Uber Rare Cat)|Shitakiri Sparrow]] - This units curse and [[Mini-Wave]] chance can work quite well here as a way to prevent the Winged Pigge from being an issue, it also has good up time.
*Any [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]] - They work incredibly well here, and the Immunity to Waves that most of them possess is the cherry on top. [[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli, Daughter of Chaos]] works best here due to her [[Curse]] being able to disable this stage completely.
*[[Togeluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Shishilan Pasalan]] - outranging every enemy here and having wave immune allow him to safely deal damage. As one of the highest damaging units with these two traits, it makes him the perfect attacker for this stage. High knockback count allows for greater leniency for winged pigge pushing. Long foreswing also makes the weaken from winged pigge have no major effect on shishilan pasalan. Once it gets rid of one of the pig threats, which should take only a few hits, the stage is over.

==Trivia==
*A clink is another term for a jail cell, derived from a particularly infamous prison in Southwark, England known as [[wikipedia:The Clink|The Clink]].

